{title: 333 - On Jordan's Banks the Baptist's Cry}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #333 • PUER NOBIS • L.M.}
{lyricist: Charles Coffin}
{composer: Michael Praetorius}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 333}
{meta: tune PUER NOBIS}
{meta: meter L.M.}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]On Jordan's [F#m]banks [G]the [F#m]Baptist's [D]cry
[D]Announces [A7]that [Bm]the [F#m/C#]Lord [D]is nigh;
[A]Awake [D]and [F#m/C#]hearken, [Bm]for he [A]brings
[G]Glad [A]tidings [Em]of [F#m]the [D]King [C#dim]of [D]kings!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Then cleansed be [Em]every [F#m]life [Em]from [D]sin;
[D]Make straight [A7]the way [Bm]for [F#m/C#]God [D]within,
[A]And [D]let us [F#m/C#]all [A]our [Bm]hearts prepare
[G]For [A]Christ [F#m]to [Em]come [F#m]and [D]enter there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]We hail [Em]You [F#m]as [G]our [F#m]Savior, [D]Lord,
[D]Our refuge [A7]and [Bm]our [F#m/C#]great [D]reward;
[A]Without [D]Your [F#m/C#]grace [A]we [Bm]waste away
[G]Like [A]flow'rs [F#m]that [Em]wither [D]and [C#dim]decay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Stretch forth [Em]Your [F#m]hand, [G]our [F#m]health [Em]restore,
[D]And make [A7]us rise [Bm]to [F#m/C#]fall [D]no more;
[A]Oh, [D]let Your [F#m/C#]face [A]upon [Bm]us [A]shine
[G]And [A]fill [F#m]the [Em]world [F#m]with [D]love [C#dim]divine.
{end_of_verse}
